// Host Core profile — the neutral base layer every host profile.jsonc is
// resolved over (ADR 0036, ADR 0057). It is also the Guided Installer's blank
// baseline, so it declares nothing personal (ADR 0157): no packages, no Host
// Programs. The operator's software lives in the Fleet Layer
// (hosts/fleet/profile.jsonc), which only `desktop` and `laptop` fold.
//
// What every install gets regardless lives with the installer, not here: the
// Base Package List, the derived sets (kernel, bootloader, filesystem, desktop,
// toggle-derived services such as cups, ADR 0079) and the Font Catalog
// defaults (ADR 0080).
//
// Resolution is per-key (ADR 0057): users/sysctl are additive, ordered
// selections (kernel, locale, desktop) are replaced.
{
  "users": [],
  "sysctl": {
    "vm.swappiness": 10
  }
}
